13. SCHEDULED DISPATCH ENGINE

A confirmed future delivery does not necessarily have an assigned courier immediately.

ROVA must distinguish between:

* Reservation confirmed.
* Courier search not started.
* Courier search in progress.
* Courier assigned.
* Courier assignment confirmed.
* Courier preparing for pickup.
* Courier en route.
* Pickup completed.
* Delivery in progress.
* Delivery completed.

The system must not tell customers that a courier is assigned when no courier has actually accepted and been assigned.

Assignment timing

Inspect the existing dispatch system.

Determine when scheduled deliveries should enter courier assignment.

Potential strategies:

* Assign in advance where operationally appropriate.
* Dispatch closer to the scheduled pickup window.
* Search earlier when the zone or vehicle category has limited capacity.
* Reassign automatically if a courier cancels.
* Escalate if no courier is found within the configured assignment deadline.

The timing must be configurable.

Do not assign couriers months or hours in advance without considering the operational consequences.

Assignment eligibility

A courier must meet the requirements of the scheduled delivery.

Consider:

* Courier status.
* Courier availability.
* Vehicle.
* Vehicle capacity.
* Location.
* Estimated arrival at pickup.
* Existing delivery assignments.
* Schedule conflicts.
* Expected completion of previous deliveries.
* Rest or operating constraints where applicable.
* Service area.
* Delivery-specific requirements.

Assignment must be atomic.

Two concurrent assignment processes must not assign the same courier to conflicting missions.

